    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.clue\n\n### Description\n\n_Taken from the [beta issue](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/issues/430#issuecomment-1703956093)._\r\n\r\nWhen using this plugin together with [`nvim-treesitter-context`](https://github.com/nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter-context), the context window disappears when `mini.clue` opens:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/62502207/66a54424-6ccf-47db-87f2-2ec43e5bc218\r\n\n\n### Neovim version\n\nv0.10.0-dev-1031+gc431d820e\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Install both `mini.clue` and [`nvim-treesitter-context`](https://github.com/nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter-context).\r\n2. Use the default settings for both plugins.\r\n3. Navigate to a position in a file of your choice that causes the window from `nvim-treesitter-context` to be opened. Type the leader key so that `mini.clue` opens.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe window from `nvim-treesitter-context` remains opened.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nThe window from `nvim-treesitter-context` is closed.\r\n\r\nAs further context, this doesn't happen with `which-key` or `nvim-cmp`, since they both use `noautocmd` in their window options: https://github.com/folke/which-key.nvim/blob/7ccf476ebe0445a741b64e36c78a682c1c6118b7/lua/which-key/view.lua#L70, https://github.com/hrsh7th/nvim-cmp/blob/5dce1b778b85c717f6614e3f4da45e9f19f54435/lua/cmp/utils/window.lua#L124.\r\n\r\nMoreover, adding `win_config.noautocmd = true` below line 1523 in this code fixes the issue.\r\nhttps://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/3a3e19d7b7850e711485b8adde73ba44789f2cf6/lua/mini/clue.lua#L1521-L1526\r\n\r\n",
